    "at": "2026-10-09T08:12:01.581Z",
    "goal": "Audit the evidence for the ArtCraft / DeepSeek information-diffusion analogy independently. Inventory and read the saved case and movement datasets, acquire one fresh hacker-discussion search and one financial-news search, recompute NVDA/QQQ around 2025-01-27 (event r1) and ADBE/QQQ around 2026-10-07 (event artcraft). Try fetching https://deepseek.com/en/news/deepseek-r1/ and, if substantive article text is available, classify its framing with Jev. Publish your own concise report and separate proposal with observations, strongest counterargument, what would change the decision and unresolved data gaps. Metadata is not full article evidence; do not treat the authored decision as truth. Do not trade or overwrite the saved case.",
    "id": "t-17",
    "network": 7,
    "report": {
      "baseHash": "6bf367de2c2c80b135c3d0aa35bdbfbf4198833d568acf909c84ac4eff2469f9",
      "file": "data/runs/t-17/report-9d9b567b1ccd.bl.org",
      "findings": [
        {
          "kind": "observation",
          "sources": [
            "A1",
            "S7",
            "D-movement"
          ],
          "text": "NVDA fell 16.97% on 2025-01-27 versus QQQ −2.91%; against a pre-event OLS fit (n=80, beta 1.51) the event residual was −12.64% on 4.08× normal volume. DeepSeek's release page states MIT-licensed weights and API pricing of $0.14/$0.55/$2.19 per million cache-hit/cache-miss/output tokens."
        },
        {
          "kind": "observation",
          "sources": [
            "A2",
            "S8",
            "S9",
            "D-movement"
          ],
          "text": "At the 2026-10-07 ArtCraft anchor ADBE fell 2.25% versus QQQ −0.25% (residual −2.55%, volume 1.23×); the next session reversed +3.56%, leaving a two-day CAR of +0.21%. The 20-session relative return to 2026-10-08 was −8.72%. Fitted ADBE beta was −0.46, i.e. unstable."
        },
        {
          "kind": "observation",
          "sources": [
            "S5",
            "S6",
            "S11",
            "D-movement"
          ],
          "text": "Fresh searches returned metadata only: one HN story (144 points, 209 comments) and four news items dated 2026-10-07/08; a later news query returned zero items. Direct fetches of AP, Phoronix and PetaPixel were HTTP 403, so their text is unavailable."
        },
        {
          "kind": "inference",
          "sources": [
            "A1",
            "A2",
            "D-case"
          ],
          "text": "The analogy is asymmetric. R1 produced immediate sector-level repricing in a supplier exposed to a capex narrative; ArtCraft produced a small one-day residual that reversed inside a longer pre-existing ADBE downtrend. The R1 template does not transfer to Adobe."
        },
        {
          "kind": "observation",
          "sources": [
            "D-movement",
            "D-case"
          ],
          "text": "The broad software-disruption narrative was public before ArtCraft: reporting of a February 2026 software selloff, and a 2026-10-07 publisher table showing the design/creative-tools median forward P/E at 15.4 versus 24.2 at the start of 2026 (sector bucket, not Adobe's multiple)."
        },
        {
          "kind": "gap",
          "sources": [
            "A3",
            "D-sentiment",
            "D-case",
            "D-movement"
          ],
          "text": "Unresolved: no borrow or options quotes, no cancellation cohort, no independent production-parity benchmark, no text for the 403-blocked publishers, no recomputation of the February 2026 baseline in this draft, and unstable ADBE beta limiting residual interpretation. Jev tone classifications cover a deliberately selected corpus, not population sentiment."
        }
      ],
      "next": [
        "Run matched non-event placebo windows and IGV/peer controls on the 2026-10-07 ADBE residual to separate sector repricing from any Adobe-specific component.",
        "Obtain authorized borrow/recall terms, options surface and a defined loss budget and horizon before any trade review.",
        "Obtain independent parity/workflow benchmarks and creator trials for the ArtCraft suite versus Adobe and existing free alternatives (GIMP 3.0, Resolve).",
        "Timestamp investor-expectation evidence (earnings-call language, analyst revisions, dated financial coverage) to test whether ArtCraft was incremental to pre-existing AI pessimism."
      ],
      "proposal": "data/runs/t-17/report-9d9b567b1ccd-proposal.bl.org",
      "summary": "Independent audit of the ArtCraft/DeepSeek analogy using the saved case, movement, sentiment and snapshot datasets plus fresh searches, prices and one Jev classification. R1's repricing is real and large; no Adobe-specific ArtCraft effect is identified. R1 is supplier-exposure evidence (NVDA), not a direct model-vendor return, and does not transfer mechanically to Adobe. Strongest counterargument: ADBE's −8.72% 20-session relative decline could be early repricing rather than noise. Conclusion: the analogy does not carry an Adobe short thesis; the authored decision remains unconfirmed and needs human source review.",
      "title": "ArtCraft × DeepSeek information-diffusion analogy: bounded independent audit"
    },
